{"name":"Fist of the North Star","hex":"#225599","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hand with the fingers clenched or curled inward.","Synonym of manicule."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strike with the fist.","To close (the hand) into a fist."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fist"},{"term":"north","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The direction towards the pole to the left-hand side of someone facing east, specifically 0°, or (on another celestial object) the direction towards the pole lying on the northern side of the invariable plane.","The up or positive direction."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the north; northern.","Toward the north; northward."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/north"},{"term":"star","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any small, natural and bright dot in the sky, most visible in the night or twilight sky. This sense includes the planets, but it is now sometimes used in exclusion of them due to influence from the technical astronomical sense.","A planet thought to influence one's fate; (figuratively) fate or luck."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To appear as a featured performer or headliner, especially in an entertainment program.","To feature (a performer or a headliner), especially in a movie or an entertainment program."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/star"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fist of the North Star","blocks":[{"text":"Fist of the North Star  is a Japanese manga series written by Buronson and illustrated by Tetsuo Hara. It was serialized in Shueisha's shōnen manga magazine Weekly Shōnen Jump for 245 issues published from 1983 to 1988 and collected in 27 tankōbon volumes under the Jump Comics imprint. Set on a post-apocalyptic Earth after a nuclear war, the story centers on a warrior named Kenshiro, the successor to a deadly martial art known as Hokuto Shinken, which gives him the ability to kill his opponents by striking their vital points, often resulting in an exceptionally violent and gory death. Kenshiro dedicates his life to fighting against the various gangs, bandits, and warlords who threaten the lives of the defenseless and innocent, as well as rival martial artists."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ce/Fist_of_the_North_Star_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fist_of_the_North_Star"},{"title":"Fist of the North Star (1986 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Fist of the North Star  is a 1986 Japanese animated post-apocalyptic martial arts film based on the manga of the same name. It was produced by Toei Animation, the same studio who worked on the TV series that was airing at the time, with most of the same cast and crew working on both projects."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3c/Hokuto_no_Ken_%281986_movie_pamphlet%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fist_of_the_North_Star_(1986_film)"},{"title":"Polaris","blocks":[{"text":"Polaris is a yellow supergiant star in the northern circumpolar constellation of Ursa Minor. It is designated α Ursae Minoris and is commonly called the North Star. With an apparent magnitude that fluctuates around 1.98, it is the brightest star in the constellation and is readily visible to the naked eye at night. The position of the star lies less than 1° away from the north celestial pole, making it the current northern pole star. The stable position of the star in the Northern Sky makes it useful for navigation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Ursa_Minor_constellation_map.svg/330px-Ursa_Minor_constellation_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polaris"},{"title":"Fist","blocks":[{"text":"A fist is the shape of a hand when the fingers are bent inward against the palm and held there tightly. To make or clench a fist is to fold the fingers tightly into the center of the palm and then to clamp the thumb over the middle phalanges; in contrast to this \"closed\" fist, one keeps the fist \"open\" by holding the thumb against the side of the index finger. One uses the closed fist to punch the lower phalanges against a surface, or to pound with the little-finger side of the hand's heel; one uses the open fist to knock with the middle knuckle of the middle finger."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fist"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg/500px-Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg/1280px-Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg/500px-Polaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Polaris components as seen by the Hubble Space Telescope","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APolaris_alpha_ursae_minoris.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/AlphaUMiLightCurve.png/500px-AlphaUMiLightCurve.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/AlphaUMiLightCurve.png/1280px-AlphaUMiLightCurve.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/AlphaUMiLightCurve.png/500px-AlphaUMiLightCurve.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"